        <body>
            <div type="edition" xml:lang="lzh" xml:space="preserve">
<ab>
<lb n="1"/><persName>大 沙門 僧安</persName>，<unclear>又</unclear><unclear>义</unclear><unclear>氏</unclear>名<persName>道壹</persName>，廣大鄉<unclear>空</unclear><unclear>□</unclear><unclear>佛</unclear><unclear>嶺</unclear>
<lb n="2"/><unclear>寬</unclear><unclear>□</unclear><unclear>□□</unclear>里人也。<unclear>寂 □</unclear><unclear>□□</unclear><unclear>寂</unclear>三世，若積石之
<lb n="3"/>千峰;<unclear>公</unclear><unclear>□</unclear><unclear>大</unclear>體<unclear>□</unclear><unclear>肥</unclear><unclear>碩</unclear><unclear>□</unclear>， <unclear>並</unclear><unclear>□</unclear><unclear>业</unclear><unclear>北</unclear>崆峒之萬<unclear>嵿</unclear><unclear>嶺</unclear>。
<lb n="4"/>嶕崔嶢道徳，器度風流。乃為詞曰：
<lb n="5"/>重疊王<unclear>寶</unclear><unclear>□</unclear><unclear>摩</unclear> ，<unclear>□</unclear><unclear>摩</unclear><unclear>日</unclear><unclear>曰</unclear><unclear>月</unclear><unclear>□</unclear>磨義，石石儁銘，
<lb n="6"/> 山山<unclear>□□</unclear>。<supplied reason="lost">雙</supplied>林<supplied reason="lost">後</supplied>一千<supplied reason="lost">六百</supplied><unclear>□□</unclear><supplied reason="lost">年</supplied>。 
</ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus"/>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                <p>The Great Renunciant ( śramaṇa ) Seng’an , also named Daoyi , is a man of the neighborhood of Empty Immensity within the village of Vast Enormity. He is quiescent [...] [within] the Three Times, like the thousand peaks of Amassed Stones. Sire’s substance is [...] and colossal, like the myriad summits of Empty Undividedness. How majestic is his virtue! How unfettered is his genius! Thus we make a verse saying: He piles up jades and jewels, [day after] day he polishes the principle. On stone after stone he chisels and carves. On mountain after mountain he [ . . . ] [ . . . ]. One thousand six hundred [ ... ] [ ... ] years after [Śākyamuni entered into nirvana under] the twin trees.</p>
            </div>
